{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1779312673,"nonce":"V+6FLn1DO8ZWt2QXJpnTUA7jAlk=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABCx-uY8680BP1"},"target":"9f9c799f5e72984d65e69129548b9b8e4fd5a9792dc475e2502af4bc3d359c39","message":"## Observation\n\n`/diagnostics_agg` on the operator station declares four `/Operator/*` rollup buckets that are all **STALE**:\n\n- `/Operator/MikroTik`\n- `/Operator/Ping`\n- `/Operator/Starlink`\n- `/Operator/Teltonika`\n\nDocumented in salmon log §10 + §12 of the [2026-05-19 deployment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135).\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe real publishers — operator-side `mikrotik_monitor`, `ping_monitor`, `starlink_diagnostics`, `teltonika_monitor` — publish their `DiagnosticStatus` entries under `/Other/...` (e.g., `/Other/ping_monitor: ping.op: ...`, `/Other/mikrotik_monitor: wifi.bizzy: ...`), not under `/Operator/...`.\n\nThe diagnostics aggregator config still expects `/Operator/*` paths and finds nothing → all 4 buckets STALE. Pre-existing config drift, not introduced today.\n\n## Independent of #3 / `ros2_network_monitor#23`\n\nEven if the operator-side `mikrotik_monitor` + `teltonika_monitor` weren't crashing on startup ([ros2_network_monitor#23](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/23)), the `/Operator/*` buckets would still be STALE because the aggregator's path map is wrong. The `starlink_diagnostics` and `ping_monitor` bucket entries are stale right now despite those two monitors being alive and publishing.\n\n## Fix options\n\n1. **Update the aggregator path map** — point `/Operator/MikroTik` etc. at the actual `/Other/{mikrotik,teltonika,starlink,ping}_monitor: *` paths. Smallest change.\n2. **Rename the aggregator buckets** to `/Other/*` style so they match where publishers land. Equivalent to dropping the `/Operator/*` rollup and relying on `/Other`.\n3. **Relocate publishers** to publish under `/Operator/*` directly. Bigger change; touches `ros2_network_monitor`. Probably overkill unless there's a wider intent to namespace operator-side diagnostics.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Toplevel `/diagnostics_agg` is driven to STALE/ERROR by these dead buckets, masking real warnings/errors elsewhere.\n- Operator loses faith in the toplevel summary when it's always wrong — they have to drill down every time.\n\n## Repo\n\n`unh_echoboats_project11` — where the BizzyBoat diagnostics_aggregator config lives (`bizzyboat_project11/config/...`).\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`\n\n---\n\n## Reframe 2026-05-20: remove the aggregator, don't fix the buckets\n\nAfter a closer look at the operator UI's diagnostic consumers, the right answer isn't any of the three fix options above — it's **remove the `diagnostic_aggregator` from operator launches entirely**.\n\n**Why:**\n\n- The annunciator (`rqt_operator_tools/annunciator_widget.py:259-297`) subscribes to `/diagnostics` directly, not to `/diagnostics_agg`. Aggregator output has no user-facing consumer in our operator UI.\n- The rqt aggregator view plugin caused stability problems in earlier sessions and we don't use it.\n- Direction in the architecture is \"publishers → `/diagnostics` → annunciator,\" with no aggregator middleman.\n\n**Action:**\n\n1. Strip the `diagnostic_aggregator` Node from `bizzyboat_project11/launch/operator_core_launch.py` (or wherever it's being instantiated in the operator launch tree — verify path before editing).\n2. Delete or move-to-historical the unused aggregator block in `bizzyboat_project11/config/diagnostics.yaml` — the `/Operator/*` analyzer config that this issue originally proposed to fix.\n\n**What this eliminates:**\n\n- The \"STALE bucket / config drift\" misdirection that wasted time during 2026-04-27 + 2026-05-19 sessions. Operators see exactly the diagnostics that publishers emit, no synthetic STALE entries.\n- Toplevel `/diagnostics_agg` driven to STALE/ERROR by dead buckets, masking real signal.\n\n**What stays:**\n\n- The publishers — `mikrotik_monitor`, `ping_monitor`, `starlink_diagnostics`, `teltonika_monitor` — keep publishing to `/diagnostics`. No change to their paths.\n- The annunciator UI's behavior is unchanged because it never used `/diagnostics_agg`.\n- If a future need for an aggregator-analyzer-based topic-staleness layer (see roadmap § Class-day operator observability \"Future\" bullet) materializes, the analyzer module can be used standalone without running the aggregator node.\n\n**Timeline:** Must finish before 2026-06-04 — Summer Hydro 2026 class start. Small change (one Node deletion + one YAML cleanup); easy win to land alongside the other small observability items (#139, #140, ros2_network_monitor#23).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779230434,"nonce":"anMvV/1/8Jc0m6fbXO3F0exDVnY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABCx-uY88AAAAF_aSd0Q"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779245836,"nonce":"xC5qHPvRpR2f/UYUGaEcll4l4/4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABC95djw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/141#issuecomment-4494089615"},"message":"## 2026-05-19 post-mission analysis: scope expansion\n\nBag analysis of the 2026-05-19 deployment (boat-side `bizzyboat` bag, ~2h 8m, 2.5M messages) surfaces a related-but-broader diagnostics aggregator problem that fits under this issue's umbrella. Headline:\n\n### `Nav2 lifecycle_manager` already publishes ERROR — the gap is downstream chronic noise\n\n`lifecycle_manager_navigation: Nav2 Health` published `DiagnosticStatus` ERROR **873 times at 1 Hz** during the failure window 13:14:40–13:29:13 EDT — exactly the silent-failure window from gabby log §13. The signal exists. What failed wasn't that Nav2 was silent; it was that the operator's diagnostics surface was **chronically ERROR-red from baseline noise**, so a new ERROR transition didn't stand out.\n\n### Chronic-noise inventory (today's bag)\n\nERROR-level names that were \"in ERROR\" essentially throughout the deployment:\n\n| Name | ERROR count | First seen | Last seen | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `udp_bridge: udp_bridge bizzy: operator: wifi` | 5147 | 12:21 EDT | 14:15 EDT | ERROR even when WiFi link is healthy |\n| `ping_monitor: ping.bizzy: salmon_direct` | 2520 | 12:21 | 13:55 | Persistent unreachable |\n| `ping_monitor: ping.bizzy: router_op_direct` | 2488 | 12:21 | 13:52 | Persistent unreachable |\n| `lifecycle_manager_navigation: Nav2 Health` | **873** | **13:14:40** | **13:29:13** | **The signal that should have stood out** |\n| `starlink_diagnostics: starlink.bizzy: link` | 37 | 12:24 | 13:45 | Brief, real transitions |\n| `mavros: System / UAS / Heartbeat / GPS / Battery` | 2–21 each | 12:07 | 13:30 | Startup transients (normal) |\n\nWARN-level chronic noise is similarly bad: `mavros: Mount` (7651), `mikrotik_monitor: ether{2,3,4,5}` (7640 each, unused router ports), `teltonika_monitor: mwan3/wan1` + `mwan3/mob1s2a1` (7638 each, cellular not in use).\n\n### Implication\n\nThe `/Operator/*` aggregator buckets being STALE (this issue's original framing) is one shape of the broader diagnostics-aggregator-config-drift problem. A complete fix needs both:\n\n1. The original `/Operator/*` path-map repair (this issue's scope)\n2. Chronic-ERROR/WARN hygiene: reclassify or threshold-tune these so they don't fire when nothing operationally is wrong. Specifically:\n   - `udp_bridge: operator: wifi` shouldn't be ERROR when WiFi link state is the intended mode (per memory `wifi_disconnect_not_an_error` — link-down is a valid operating mode, not an error)\n   - Unused router ports (`ether2-5`) and unused cellular interfaces shouldn't fire WARN — either filter at publisher or rebucket in aggregator\n   - `ping_monitor` targets that don't reflect operational reality (e.g., `salmon_direct`, `router_op_direct` that were unreachable throughout) should be removed or reconfigured — sibling work to [`#140`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/140) (`bencloud` ping)\n   - `mavros: Mount` (\"Can not diagnose in this targeting mode\") fires 7651 times — should be one-shot INFO or filtered\n\nWithout (2), even fixing (1) leaves the operator's toplevel rollup permanently in WARN/ERROR — which is what desensitized them to today's real `Nav2 Health` ERROR transition.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nSuggest reframing this issue's scope from \"/Operator/* aggregator buckets STALE\" to \"diagnostics aggregator surface needs config hygiene\". Or split into two issues — the original `/Operator/*` repair + a new \"chronic-noise hygiene\" tracker. Either way the brainstorm conclusion in [`rolker/ros2launch_session#5`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2launch_session/issues/5) shifts — the narrow Nav2 annunciator sub-task there is partially redundant because Nav2 already does the publishing; what matters is making sure the annunciator panel isn't already-red from chronic noise when Nav2 fires its real ERROR.\n\n### Source\n\nBoat-side bag SQLite at `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-19/bizzyboat.db`. Query that produced the table above:\n\n```sql\nWITH err_names AS (\n  SELECT t_ns, value as name FROM t_diagnostics,\n         json_each('[\"' || REPLACE(error_names, '|', '\",\"') || '\"]')\n  WHERE n_error \u003e 0\n)\nSELECT name, COUNT(*), MIN(t_ns), MAX(t_ns)\nFROM err_names GROUP BY name ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC;\n```\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1779312673,"nonce":"4taBuzM6u4PLZL3QtibBczjQYSw=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABCx-uY88AAAAGAH9zMw"},"title":"Remove diagnostic_aggregator from operator launches (annunciator uses /diagnostics directly)","was":"Remove diagnostic_aggregator from operator launches (annunciator uses /diagnostics directly)"},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779372190,"nonce":"JCMVpida2AcPXS4YH4AcVc9r4AQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABCx-uY88AAAAGAkbHpQ"},"status":2}]}